content.text:
The answer is a single root cause: ts-travel-plan-service, with an `http_slow` fault on its outgoing GET calls to ts-train-service. The seat-service stalls are real but too rare and too unlike a systematic fault to name, so I left them out.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name AS caller, c.span_name AS client_span, s.service_name AS callee, s.span_name AS server_span, count(*) AS n, approx_quantile(c.duration/1e6,0.5) AS client_p50_ms, approx_quantile(s.duration/1e6,0.5) AS server_p50_ms, approx_quantile(c.duration/1e6,0.05) AS client_p05_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id = c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name = 'ts-travel-plan-service' AND c.attr_span_kind = 'Client' AND s.service_name = 'ts-train-service' GROUP BY 1,2,3,4",
          "claim": "Travel-plan GET calls to train-service take about 613 ms client-side while train-service server spans take about 3.5 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name AS caller, c.span_name AS client_span, s.service_name AS callee, count(*) AS n, approx_quantile(c.duration/1e6,0.5) AS client_p50_ms, approx_quantile(s.duration/1e6,0.5) AS server_p50_ms FROM normal_traces c JOIN normal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id = c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name = 'ts-travel-plan-service' AND c.attr_span_kind = 'Client' AND s.service_name = 'ts-train-service' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "In the normal period the same travel-plan GET to train-service took about 6 ms client-side, with server time unchanged."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) AS n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.5) AS p50_ms, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'ts-travel-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind = 'Client' GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY 2",
          "claim": "Only travel-plan's GET client spans are held back; its POST client spans to other services are unchanged from normal."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_span_kind, span_name, count(*) AS n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE attr_span_kind = 'Server' AND span_name LIKE 'POST /api/v1/travelplanservice%' GROUP BY 1,2,3 ORDER BY 3",
          "claim": "The dashboard's travel-plan server spans run about 1–3.5 s at p95, tracking the slowed travel-plan server spans behind them."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
